associated primes
*****************

The function *note associatedPrimes: associatedPrimes, returns a list of the
associated prime ideals for a given ideal I. The associated prime ideals
correspond to the irreducible components of the variety associated to I. They
are useful in many applications in commutative algebra, algebraic geometry and
combinatorics.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..d];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a*b-c*d, (a*c-b*d)^2);                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : associatedPrimes I                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {ideal (d, a), ideal (c, b), ideal (b - c, a - d), ideal (b + c, a + d)}|
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See *note primary decomposition: primary decomposition, for more information
about finding primary decompositions. To find just the minimal prime ideals see
*note minimal primes of an ideal: (MinimalPrimes)minimal primes of an ideal,.



