localize -- localize an ideal at a prime ideal
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        localize(I, P)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a (quotient of a)
        polynomial ring R
      * P, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a prime ideal in the same ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value 1
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the extension contraction ideal
        $I R_P \cap R$.

Description
===========

The result is the ideal obtained by first extending to the localized ring and
then contracting back to the original ring.

+-------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/(101)[x,y];  |
+-------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal (x^2,x*y);|
|                         |
|o2 : Ideal of R          |
+-------------------------+
|i3 : P1 = ideal (x);     |
|                         |
|o3 : Ideal of R          |
+-------------------------+
|i4 : localize(I,P1)      |
|                         |
|o4 = ideal x             |
|                         |
|o4 : Ideal of R          |
+-------------------------+
|i5 : P2 = ideal (x,y);   |
|                         |
|o5 : Ideal of R          |
+-------------------------+
|i6 : localize(I,P2)      |
|                         |
|             2           |
|o6 = ideal (x , x*y)     |
|                         |
|o6 : Ideal of R          |
+-------------------------+
+----------------------------+
|i7 : R = ZZ/31991[x,y,z];   |
+----------------------------+
|i8 : I = ideal(x^2,x*z,y*z);|
|                            |
|o8 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+
|i9 : P1 = ideal(x,y);       |
|                            |
|o9 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+
|i10 : localize(I,P1)        |
|                            |
|o10 = ideal (y, x)          |
|                            |
|o10 : Ideal of R            |
+----------------------------+
|i11 : P2 = ideal(x,z);      |
|                            |
|o11 : Ideal of R            |
+----------------------------+
|i12 : localize(I,P2)        |
|                            |
|                 2          |
|o12 = ideal (z, x )         |
|                            |
|o12 : Ideal of R            |
+----------------------------+

The strategy option value should be one of the following, with default value 1.

  * Strategy => 0 -- Uses the algorithm of Eisenbud-Huneke-Vasconcelos

    This strategy does not require the calculation of the assassinator, but can
    require the computation of high powers of ideals. The method appears in
    Eisenbud-Huneke-Vasconcelos, Invent. Math. 110 (1992) 207-235.
  * Strategy => 1 -- Uses a separator to find the localization

    This strategy uses a separator polynomial - a polynomial in all of the
    associated primes of {   t I} but {      t P} and those contained in {   t
    P}. In this strategy, the assassinator of the ideal will be recalled, or
    recomputed using *note Strategy => 1: associatedPrimes, if unknown. The
    separator polynomial method is described in Shimoyama-Yokoyama, J. Symbolic
    computation, 22(3) 247-277 (1996). This is the same as Strategy => 1 except
    that, if unknown, the assassinator is computed using *note Strategy => 2:
    associatedPrimes,.
  * Strategy => 2 -- Uses a separator to find the localization

Authored by C. Yackel (see http://faculty.mercer.edu/yackel_ca ). Last modified
June, 2000.

Caveat
======

The ideal P is not checked to be prime.

See also
========

  * *note primaryDecomposition(Ideal): primaryDecomposition, -- irredundant
    primary decomposition of an ideal
  * *note radical: (MinimalPrimes)radical, -- the radical of an ideal
  * *note minimalPrimes: (MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes, -- minimal primes of an
    ideal
  * *note topComponents: topComponents, -- compute top dimensional component of
    an ideal or module
  * *note removeLowestDimension: removeLowestDimension, -- remove components of
    lowest dimension

Ways to use localize:
=====================

  * "localize(Ideal,Ideal)"

