Strategy => Hybrid{associated primes strategy, localize strategy}
=================================================================

Uses a hybrid of the Eisenbud-Huneke-Vasconcelos and Shimoyama-Yokoyama
strategies. To use this strategy, the field Strategy should be a list of two
integers, indicating the strategy to use for finding associated primes and
localizing, respectively.

Warning: Setting the second parameter to 1 works only if the ideal is
homogeneous and equidimensional.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Q = QQ[x,y];                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : I = intersect(ideal(x^2), ideal(y^2))            |
|                                                      |
|            2 2                                       |
|o8 = ideal(x y )                                      |
|                                                      |
|o8 : Ideal of Q                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : primaryDecomposition(I, Strategy => Hybrid{1,1}) |
|                                                      |
|             2         2                              |
|o9 = {ideal x , ideal y }                             |
|                                                      |
|o9 : List                                             |
